      "explanation": "Explanation:\nTo put the green cubes together, we first need to identify the green cubes in the scene. In this case, they are obj3 and obj4. Their initial positions are [0.178, -0.042] and [0.215, 0.104] respectively.\n\nWe compute the direction vector from obj3 to obj4, which is [0.215 - 0.178, 0.104 - (-0.042)] = [0.037, 0.146]. The Euclidean distance between them is sqrt(0.037^2 + 0.146^2) = 0.150.\n\nWe choose a scaling factor \u03b1 = 0.5. We multiply the direction vector by \u03b1 to get the offset [0.037 * 0.5, 0.146 * 0.5] = [0.0185, 0.073]. We add this offset to the position of obj3 to get the target position [0.178 + 0.0185, -0.042 + 0.073, 0.8] = [0.1965, 0.031, 0.8].\n\nThis target position is the point in the straight line between obj3 and obj4 where we want to move obj3. The final distance between obj3 and obj4 will be 0.150 - 0.5 * 0.150 = 0.075, which is greater than 0.07, so there will be no collision.\n\nThe symbolic plan is then to move the robot arm to obj3, grip and pick up obj3, move obj3 to the target position, and then open the gripper to release obj3.",
